      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subjects offered in the term '2017JA': TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- Chemistry department: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- Course 5: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- subject ID: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\n- subject title: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- offering department code: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- offering department name: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\n- number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- department full name: STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME\n- school name: STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME\n- minimum number of enrolled students over each department code group: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the year 2022: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS, SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- excluding the Biology department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- degree-granting departments: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- average number of enrolled students for subjects offered by that department in the year 2022: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TERM_CODE, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n\n## Join Keys\n- STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"Chemistry\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry'\"\n- \"degree-granting\" is predicated by \"TABLE.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"\n- \"Course 5\" is predicated by \"TABLE.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = '5'\"\n- \"Biology\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '7'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For subjects offered in the term '2017JA' by the Chemistry department (Course 5), show the subject ID, subject title, offering department code, offering department name, number of enrolled students, department full name, school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each department code group, ordered by department code, and only include subjects where the offering department name is 'Chemistry'.\n```sql\nSELECT t0.SUBJECT_ID, t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, t1.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, t1.SCHOOL_NAME, min(t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (PARTITION BY t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE ORDER BY t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE) AS min_enrolled_students FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN STUDENT_DEPARTMENT t1 ON t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2017JA' AND t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' AND t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = '5'\n```\n2. For each department, give the department name and the variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the year 2022, but only include departments that grant degrees and exclude the Biology department (Course 7).\n```sql\nSELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, VARIANCE(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED cso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON cso.DEPARTMENT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = sos.OFFER_DEPT_CODE WHERE cso.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '7' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY total_units_variance DESC;\n```\n3. For subjects offered in the term '2017JA' by the Chemistry department (Course 5), show the subject ID, subject title, offering department code, offering department name, number of enrolled students, department full name, school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each department code group. Additionally, for each such subject, include the department name and the variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the year 2022, but only include departments that grant degrees and exclude the Biology department (Course 7). Order the results by department code and variance of total units in descending order.\n```sql\nWITH ChemistrySubjects AS ( SELECT t0.SUBJECT_ID, t0.SUBJECT_TITLE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE, t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, t1.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, t1.SCHOOL_NAME, min(t0.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (PARTITION BY t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE ORDER BY t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE) AS min_enrolled_students FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t0 JOIN STUDENT_DEPARTMENT t1 ON t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE t0.TERM_CODE = '2017JA' AND t0.OFFER_DEPT_NAME = 'Chemistry' AND t0.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = '5' ), DepartmentUnitsVariance AS ( SELECT sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, VARIANCE(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance, sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED cso JOIN SIS_DEPARTMENT sd ON cso.DEPARTMENT_CODE = sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE = sos.OFFER_DEPT_CODE WHERE cso.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND sd.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '7' GROUP BY sd.DEPARTMENT_NAME, sd.DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY total_units_variance DESC ) SELECT cs.SUBJECT_ID, cs.SUBJECT_TITLE, cs.OFFER_DEPT_CODE, cs.OFFER_DEPT_NAME, cs.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, cs.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, cs.SCHOOL_NAME, cs.min_enrolled_students, duv.DEPARTMENT_NAME, duv.total_units_variance FROM ChemistrySubjects cs JOIN DepartmentUnitsVariance duv ON cs.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = duv.DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY cs.OFFER_DEPT_CODE, duv.total_units_variance DESC;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor subjects offered in the term '2017JA' by the Chemistry department (Course 5), show the subject ID, subject title, offering department code, offering department name, number of enrolled students, department full name, school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each department code group. Additionally, for each such subject, include the department name, the variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the year 2022 (excluding the Biology department and only including degree-granting departments), and the average number of enrolled students for subjects offered by that department in the year 2022. Order the results by department code and variance of total units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers."
